Linux supports audio playback out of the box through ALSA (Advanced Linux Sound
Architecture). For even slightly more complex use cases, you will most likely
want to use a more advanced audio framework such as PipeWire. PipeWire can be
used as an audio server providing compatibility layers for ALSA and PulseAudio.

If you intend to use a window manager or compositor, you almost certainly will
require sound features beyond those provided by ALSA. As PipeWire is still
relatively new, we will also set up rerouting of ALSA and PulseAudio sound
signals through PipeWire. This ensures compatibility with virtually all
applications. PipeWire also supports JACK, but as a more advanced audio
solution, rerouting of JACK audio is not covered by this script.
